.SH NAME
daharness\-safety \(em daharness safety model: scope gate, approvals,
budgets, retention
.SH DESCRIPTION
.SS Scope gate (operator\-armed only)
Traffic\-sending tools resolve every target through an operator\-armed
scope state.
Arming happens ONLY at the operator REPL (\f[CR]scope on <handle>\f[R])
and is deliberately NOT exposed as an LLM\-callable tool, so the
secretary can never toggle it.
State persists across processes (the REPL can re\-arm a running Brain).
Blocked targets raise a scope error instead of transmitting.
.SS Human\-in\-the\-loop approval
Tool execution from the secretary is gated by an approval loop: the run
pauses until the confirmer approves the exact manifest + arguments,
capped by SECRETARY_MAX_APPROVAL_ROUNDS.
Tool calls through the API gateway or MCP bypass this lane by design
\(em those lanes carry the per\-turn budget instead.
.SS Per\-turn tool budget
Gateway lanes (REST/MCP/Open WebUI) enforce a hard cap on tool
executions per turn; the final allowed call is wrapped with a directive
to report findings and end the turn; further calls are refused with
structured guidance (not a transient error).
Terminal\-lane tools (memory, findings, unknowns) stay callable past the
cap so the model can comply.
.SS Local\-only LLM policy
The secretary runs on a locally hosted model (Ollama, loopback/LAN) \(em
never a cloud LLM API.
Tool outputs from live targets (credentials, tokens, internal IPs) must
not egress to third parties.
.SS Engagement cobweb
An engagement\(aqs rows (journal, evidence, findings, unknowns) unify
under one slug, so a purge erases one engagement in a single transaction
while the journal audit trail stays append\-only until the operator
closes it.
Arming is REPL\-only.
.SS Credential\-reuse sweep
Every recovered credential gets ONE validation attempt against each
other reachable service before deeper work resumes \(em logged as
findings, auditable in the evidence store.
